{{also|milk toast}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From the character {{w|Caspar Milquetoast}} of the comic strip ''The Timid Soul'', created by {{w|H._T._Webster|Harold Webster}} and first published in 1924 (named after the American dish {{m|en|milk toast}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪlktəʊst/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[meek|Meek]], [[timid]].
#* {{quote-journal|year=1951|author={{w|Joseph William Martin Jr.|Joseph W. Martin}}|journal=Congressional Record|volume=97|section=part 14|passage=The truth is that we are cursed with a “'''milquetoast'''” Government operating under “'''milquetoast'''” policies. Fear has become a national policy.}}
#* '''2016''', [[w:Christopher Kelly (author)|Christopher Kelly]], ''The Pink Bus''. Mapple Shade, New Jersey: Lethe Press. p. 80.
#*:And if Dick Leonard didn't appreciate Patrick's incisive criticism--if it inspired a streak of vindictiveness in his usually '''milquetoast''' boss and Dick ended up making his assistant's life miserable?

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|pejorative}} A [[person]] of [[meek]] or [[timid]] [[disposition]].

